## Data Storage and Retention

### Local Storage

Most gameplay information is stored locally on your device using browser storage technologies.

Because this information remains on your device:

* We generally cannot access it remotely.
* We cannot recover lost progress if local storage is deleted.
* Clearing browser data may permanently remove saved progress.

### Authentication Data

Authentication tokens may be stored locally for session management and are used only to verify your identity with Pi Network.

---

## Security

We implement reasonable technical and organizational safeguards designed to protect your information, including:

* HTTPS encrypted communications
* Secure authentication practices
* Limited access to system resources
* Regular security reviews and updates

While we strive to protect your information, no internet-based service can guarantee absolute security. Use of the Services is at your own risk.

